<p>In the latest development in the Middle East war, President Trump said he ordered a five-day pause on U.S. strikes against Iranian power plants and other energy infrastructure, saying the delay followed “productive” conversations and possible “major points of agreement” with Iranian officials. Iranian officials publicly rejected that account, with state-linked and parliamentary figures saying no negotiations had taken place, although a senior Iranian Foreign Ministry official later told CBS News that Tehran had received a U.S. message through mediators. The pause appeared to reduce, at least temporarily, the risk of an immediate strike on Iran’s energy grid and offered a narrow diplomatic opening in a conflict now in its fourth week. But fighting continued elsewhere: multiple reports said U.S. operations were set to continue against non-energy targets, Israel kept striking Iranian sites, and Iran launched missiles and drones toward Israel and some Gulf Arab states while maintaining pressure around the Strait of Hormuz. The mixed signals left peace prospects uncertain, yet the existence of mediator channels suggested diplomacy had not fully closed off.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/6LzBaAxsLOaVLzYK2-B6iBq-6Tk6D9HwRKHF_pKe2kwi4Z4oPsjibbxUzQlI_Iv_3qBRbvq3RLCh2W8F5jlPYwSqeno5R-K_Fwpt5r049joiHXPUHC6Bm3PQkXLKmyo50Zc9cuCflFjUbngXUjNFF1AGIsdzBFbtQICzkTyrrofcfbtYcJQ' alt='Abbas Araghchi, Iran’s foreign minister, in Tehran last year. He is said to have conveyed to the U.S. that Iran would need sanctions relief and guarantees against future attacks.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Possible format for talks: Al-Monitor reported Washington had proposed possible Vance-Ghalibaf talks, with Turkey identified by a source as one intermediary, offering the clearest picture yet of what a contact channel might look like.</li><li>Limited pause: A U.S. official told Semafor and Reuters, via Al-Monitor, that the five-day halt applies only to Iranian energy sites, while attacks on military, naval, missile and defense-industrial targets would continue.</li><li>Early-stage diplomacy: The New York Times reported officials described the contacts as early and not yet substantive, a much narrower characterization than President Trump’s claim of “major points of agreement”.</li><li>Deadline reset: The move effectively extended President Trump’s original 48-hour ultimatum tied to reopening the Strait of Hormuz into a five-day holding pattern rather than an immediate escalation.</li><li>Israel&#x27;s role: Semafor reported Israel was being updated on the U.S.-Iran contacts but was not a direct party to the talks.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: President Trump said the United States and Iran had held “very good and productive” conversations, claimed there were “major points of agreement,” and delayed attacks on Iran’s energy infrastructure for five days. (<a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/23/nx-s1-5757380/president-trump-and-iranian-officials-have-conflicting-stories-about-ongoing-talks'>NPR</a>)</li><li>Iranian Foreign Ministry official: A senior Iranian Foreign Ministry official told CBS News that Tehran had received a U.S. message through mediators, suggesting indirect communication even as public denials continued. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/iran-us-message-mediators-trump-iran-war-possible-deal/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Iranian parliament speaker Mohammad Bagher Qalibaf: Qalibaf denied Iran was negotiating with Washington and said claims of talks were “fake news” used to influence financial and oil markets. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-trump-claims-u-s-and-iran-are-holding-talks-iran-wants-to-make-a-deal'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>European Commission: Ursula von der Leyen said the global energy situation was “critical” and argued the war needed to end through negotiation rather than further escalation. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/mar/24/iran-war-live-updates-trump-ursula-von-der-leyen-oil-prices-energy-crisis-israel-strikes'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu: Netanyahu said President Trump saw a chance to convert military gains into an agreement that protects Israeli interests. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/23/2026/us-to-keep-attacking-iran-as-israel-stays-on-sidelines-of-talks'>Semafor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/23/nx-s1-5757380/president-trump-and-iranian-officials-have-conflicting-stories-about-ongoing-talks'>President Trump and Iranian officials have conflicting stories about ongoing talks</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-us-israel-trump-ultimatum-strait-of-hormuz/'>Trump calls off Strait of Hormuz ultimatum as Iran receives U.S. message from mediators</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.economist.com/middle-east-and-africa/2026/03/23/the-war-room-newsletter-trump-is-scrambling-for-options-in-iran'>The War Room newsletter: Trump is scrambling for options in Iran</a> - economist.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1s1xvka/us_sent_iran_a_message_through_mediators_as_trump/'>U.S. sent Iran a message through mediators as Trump signals he&#x27;s open to a deal, Iranian official says</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/f9f0980b-385d-4ad2-b242-3b89666282a5'>Iran contradicts Trump and says no direct talks to end war</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/mar/24/iran-war-live-updates-trump-ursula-von-der-leyen-oil-prices-energy-crisis-israel-strikes'>Middle East crisis live: Iran dismisses Trump claim of talks; von der Leyen says global energy situation is ‘critical’</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/us-continue-iran-strikes-pause-applies-only-energy-sites-semafor-reports'>US to continue Iran strikes, pause applies only to ener